    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0112" n="22" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg22"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/924</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reinsch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-09T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1918, 5 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 9, 4.45
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Moser requests authorization Drysdale<anchor n="2" xml:id="d35-f1"/>
                    proceed Siberia to gather the information on conditions there as requested your
                    instructions to him. Please instruct Moser directly.</p>
                <p>Naval attaché suggests advisability of sending to assist Drysdale a Serbian Colonel
                        Speskov, now here, available, who has offered his
                    services and is thoroughly familiar with the situation, speaking all necessary
                    languages. Please instruct me whether this and necessary expenses are
                    authorized.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Reinsch</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
